# The QTI boot control HAL. AOSP installs android.hardware.boot@1.2-service
# into recovery as a "disabled" service, so nothing ever starts it: every
# bootctl call then fails with "Error getting bootctrl v1.0 module", and a
# flashing script that switches slots afterwards silently does nothing. The
# stock vendor copy runs in class early_hal for the same reason.
#
# Unlike the security HALs this one talks to the GPT, not to a QSEE listener,
# so it only has to wait for hwservicemanager.
on property:hwservicemanager.ready=true
    start boot-hal-1-2

# One cosmetic quirk survives: get_number_slots() reports 3, because the QTI
# implementation counts by-name entries prefixed with "boot" and TWRP adds a
# bare "boot" symlink next to boot_a and boot_b. Everything load-bearing --
# current/active slot, suffixes, bootable and successful flags -- reads back
# correctly, and nothing in TWRP or a flashing script uses the slot count.
